# P3 motor feature flags. All potentially dangerous actions OFF by default.
mainmenu "nice!nano Tuya P3 Zigbee blind"
source "Kconfig.zephyr"

menu "P3 prototype features"

config P3_UART_TX_ENABLE
    bool "ENABLE real Tuya P3 motor UART transmission (hardware test only)"
    default n
    help
      WARNING: Allows real motor movement from Zigbee commands.
      Only enable after validating pinout, supply, UART startup and
      safe end-stop behavior on the real P3 installation.
      Disabled by default even when the host tests succeed.

config P3_DIAG_STARTUP_QUERIES
    bool "Send four allowlisted P3 startup diagnostic UART requests ONCE"
    default n
    help
      Diagnostic-only physical UART TX with the movement command path OFF.
      Once after UART RX is ready, sends exactly four previously captured
      classic Tuya zero-data request frames: heartbeat 0x00, product 0x01,
      work mode 0x02, status query 0x08, in that order. No repeats, movement
      commands, target positions, STOP, Wi-Fi status, or Zigbee-triggered
      transmissions are possible in this diagnostic mode. Requires safe
      hardware-level UART 3.3 V, separate supplies, common GND and actual
      P3 TXD -> nRF P0.20 connected only for supervised bench testing.
      Choose this feature WITHOUT P3_UART_TX_ENABLE or P3_MCU_INIT_ENABLE.

config P3_MCU_INIT_ENABLE
    bool "Send captured WBR3 wake initialization (no motor motion)"
    depends on P3_UART_TX_ENABLE
    default n
    help
      Replays verified startup request opcodes after UART RX initialization:
      0x00 heartbeat, 0x01 product, 0x02 mode, 0x08 DP query.
      This does NOT send any motor movement or legacy Wi-Fi state.
      Repeated heartbeat intervals were not measured, so periodic polling
      is NOT implemented. Hardware startup reliability still untested.

config P3_ZCL_POSITION_ENABLE
    bool "Expose DP3 as current lift percentage (physical polarity to verify)"
    default n
    help
      Enables Zigbee CurrentPositionLiftPercentage updates based on DP3.
      Use only after confirming DP3 is a valid 0..100 position.\n      Verify physical open/closed orientation before treating the value as\n      calibrated; reporting is read-only and cannot move the motor.

config P3_POSITION_TARGET_ENABLE
    bool "Enable experimental DP2 percentage setpoint (supervised testing only)"
    depends on P3_UART_TX_ENABLE && P3_ZCL_POSITION_ENABLE
    default n
    help
      Allows Zigbee GoToLiftPercentage to send DP2 target values to P3.
      DP2 target behavior is not yet verified on physical P3 hardware.
      Enable only on the experimental blind, with working STOP and
      a clear path to stop motor movement. Does not calibrate motor limits.

config P3_ZCL_POSITION_INVERT
    bool "Invert DP3 lift percentage and Zigbee requested setpoint"
    depends on P3_ZCL_POSITION_ENABLE
    default n
    help
      Zigbee Window Covering reports 0 percent as OPEN and 100 as CLOSED.
      Enable if actual DP3 is 0 percent CLOSED and 100 OPEN.

config P3_ZCL_BATTERY_ENABLE
    bool "Map DP13 to Zigbee Power Configuration battery percentage"
    default n
    help
      DP13=40 was observed while the battery displayed 40 percent.
      Separate runtime verification of source and calibration is required.
      Zigbee BatteryPercentageRemaining is half-percent units (40%=80).

endmenu
